course: dictionary
lesson: 586
title: Automatically: by itself, or without thinking
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Automatically» is an adverb. It tells you how something happens. Its main meaning is by itself, done by a machine without a person needing to do it. «Hospitals have generators that start automatically» means nobody has to press a button for them to start.
explain: It can also mean without thinking, out of habit. When a light flashes in your eyes, you blink automatically. You do not decide to blink, it just happens. Your heart beats automatically for the same reason.
explain: Look at the words around it to choose the right meaning. «If you are late, you automatically lose a point» means it follows as a rule, always. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «You always lose a point» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Automatically means by itself, done without a person doing it.
fact: Automatically can mean without thinking, out of habit, like blinking.
fact: «Phones update automatically» means nobody has to press a button for the update to happen.
fact: Automatically can also mean always, as a rule: «If you are late, you automatically lose a point.»
fact: «Direct debit» takes a bill from a bank account automatically, but there must be enough money in the account on the day.
exercise: «Hospitals have generators that start automatically.» What does automatically mean here? | *By itself, without a person starting them | Very slowly and carefully | With a lot of noise | Only on Sundays
exercise: Ella says, «I blinked automatically when the light flashed.» What does automatically suggest? | *Without thinking, out of habit | Never at all | Very loudly | On purpose, after a long think
exercise: «If you are late, you automatically lose a point.» Which meaning fits this sentence? | Quietly and secretly | *Always, as a rule | Only once a year | Sometimes, if you feel like it
test: «Streaming plays the next episode automatically to keep you watching.» Which phrase could replace automatically? | Once a week | By itself | *By itself, as the next episode starts | Very angrily
test: Jayden says, «My heart beats automatically.» Why does he say automatically? | He decides it again every second | *It happens without him deciding it | It only beats when he runs | It stops at night
exam: «A direct debit lets a company take a bill from the bank account automatically.» What is the best meaning of automatically here? | *Without a person needing to act each time | Late at night | With a pen and paper | Only once, never again
